      Chats userscript are governed separately by their own documents, above on this page.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2 id="rtos-description">Description of Service</h2>
    <p>
      Recruiter runs on Torn.com via a userscript manager (such as Tampermonkey) or Torn PDA and surfaces
      publicly available game data &mdash; company rosters, Hall of Fame working stats, player factions, and
      online status &mdash; to help with company recruiting. It shows which high working-stat players are
      employed in the company types you select, and whether they are online right now. The data is fetched and
      refreshed by the TornManager server; the userscript itself talks only to tornmanager.com. Recruiter
      requires an active TornManager subscription.
    </p>
    <p>By installing and using Recruiter, you agree to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Allow the userscript to display its interface on Torn.com pages in your browser</li>
      <li>Allow the userscript to communicate with tornmanager.com for sign-in, subscription checks, recruiting data, and key pool management</li>
      <li>Allow the TornManager server to call the official Torn API with the keys in the shared pool on Recruiter's behalf</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2 id="rtos-api-key">API Key &amp; Authentication</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Never share your Torn password with anyone, including me.</strong> Recruiter only requires a Torn
      API key with Public access to sign in, and accepts nothing more powerful. Signing in requires an active
      TornManager subscription. You are responsible for creating and managing your key, monitoring its usage
      through Torn.com ('key' &rarr; 'log' selection), and revoking or regenerating it if you suspect misuse. By
      signing in you explicitly authorize TornManager to verify your identity via the Torn API and to use your
      key in Recruiter's shared fetching pool, as documented in the Privacy Policy.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2 id="rtos-key-pool">Key Pool Rules</h2>
    <p>
      You may add other players' API keys to the shared pool <strong>only if their owners handed them to you
      voluntarily</strong>, knowing what they will be used for. Pool keys are stored on the TornManager server
      and used server-side for background fetching. Every call carries the comment <code>tmrecruiter</code> so
      key owners can audit usage in their own Torn key log at any time. The pool accepts only Public access keys
      and one key per player. The server paces its Torn API usage to stay well inside Torn's rate limits per key
      owner.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2 id="rtos-acceptable-use">Acceptable Use</h2>
    <p>
      Recruiter shows you public information about players; what you do with it is your responsibility. You must
      not use Recruiter to:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>harass, threaten, or spam players, whether or not they respond to a recruiting approach;</li>
      <li>violate Torn's rules or Terms of Service, including its rules on unsolicited messaging; or</li>
      <li>collect data with keys whose owners did not consent to their use.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

